{"id":587,"name":"emolga","speciesId":587,"dex":587,"form":"normal","generation":5,"types":["electric","flying"],"stats":{"hp":55,"attack":75,"defense":60,"special-attack":75,"special-defense":60,"speed":103},"abilities":[{"name":"static","hidden":false},{"name":"motor-drive","hidden":true}],"height":4,"weight":50,"baseExp":150,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/587.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/587.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/587.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/587.ogg","genus":"Sky Squirrel Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon Esquilo Celeste","flavor":[{"version":"black","text":"The energy made in its cheeks’ electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding."},{"version":"white","text":"They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity."},{"version":"black-2","text":"It glides on its outstretched membrane while shocking foes with the electricity stored in the pouches on its cheeks."},{"version":"sun","text":"It glides using its cape-like membrane. Electrical energy scatters from it, shocking its friends and foes alike."},{"version":"moon","text":"It grills berries and bug Pokémon with electric shocks and makes a meal of them. It usually nests in the holes gouged in trees by Pikipek."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"They store up electricity to fly through the air. When thunder cracks at night, sometimes there are almost enough of them to blot out the sky."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"As it flies, it scatters electricity around, so bird Pokémon keep their distance. That’s why Emolga can keep all its food to itself."},{"version":"sword","text":"As Emolga flutters through the air, it crackles with electricity. T